   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Murray and Others<br>Could you help me how to write extractfn for covariate coefficients.<br>I would like to run D~elv+ruggedness model with 50 simulation/bootstrap in sim.secr function, also I would like to see the beta coefficients for each simulation. How to get that?<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "cLHAEy8XAgAJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2017-11-16T19:12:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: Function to simulate covariate model of density",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I often use extractfn = identity and manipulate the resulting list of lists of secr fitted models, but this takes a lot of space when nrepl is large and can test your R skills. More directly, why not use the coef function?<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">## a simple example</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>scen1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> make</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scenarios</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">25</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g0 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> noccasions </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                            c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>traps1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> make</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">grid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#800\">## default 6 x 6 trap grid</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tmp1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> run</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">scenarios</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nrepl </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> trapset </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> traps1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scenarios </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scen1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">args </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> extractfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## selecting one coefficient (i.e. one row in coef table)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tmp1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> parameter </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;g0.bTRUE&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>Murray</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Friday, November 17, 2017 at 7:33:36 AM UTC+13, mayank wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi Murray and Others<br>Could you help me how to write extractfn for covariate coefficients.<br>I would like to run D~elv+ruggedness model with 50 simulation/bootstrap in sim.secr function, also I would like to see the beta coefficients for each simulation. How to get that?<br></blockquote></div>"
    ]
